<Step ID="3" Task="Using F = ma and velocity-time relation v = ∫a dt, derive the acceleration as a function of v. What is a(v)?" Difficulty="6" Token="70" Rely="2"/>
<Step ID="4" Task="Using the chain rule d/dv [v/a(v)], show that the acceleration decreases as v approaches c. How does this confirm the decreasing acceleration hypothesis?" Difficulty="7" Token="80" Rely="3"/>
<Step ID="5" Task="Given F(v) and a(v) from Steps 2 and 3, what is the final behavior of gravitational force and acceleration as v → c?" Difficulty="5" Token="60" Rely="2,3"/>
<Step ID="6" Task="What is the correct description of their motion, combining the decreasing acceleration from Step 4 and the physical constraints of relativity?" Difficulty="4" Token="40" Rely="4,5"/>
</Plan>
```

